</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Study alias structures in regular fractional factorial designs.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Construct a Resolution IV fractional factorial design.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Investigate Plackett--Burman screening designs.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Study response-surface methodology and central composite designs.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Investigate Box--Behnken designs.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Study D-optimal and A-optimal experimental designs.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Investigate rerandomization using Mahalanobis-distance balance criteria.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Study covariate-adaptive randomization.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Investigate group-sequential experiments.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Study response-adaptive randomization.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Investigate cluster-randomized trial power and sample-size formulas.</p>
